---
import ProseLayout from '../../layouts/ProseLayout.astro';
import Card from '../../components/ds/Card.astro';
import { DEMO_BOOKING_URL } from '../../config';
---
<ProseLayout
  title="Privacy information"
  metaTitle="Privacy | PumpOS"
  description="Draft privacy information and contact details for the PumpOS pilot."
  path="/legal/privacy"
  eyebrow="PumpOS pilot"
  noindex
>
  <Card as="aside" class="prose-callout" role="note">
    <p><strong>Draft.</strong> This page is waiting for founder approval and legal review. It is not a final privacy policy and has no effective date yet. Anything marked <span class="legal-tbd">To be confirmed</span> is still open.</p>
  </Card>

  {/* Hidden until PumpOS is registered. Restore with the legal name, registered address and jurisdiction.
  <h2>Who runs PumpOS</h2>
  <p>PumpOS is run by [legal name], [registered address]. [Jurisdiction].</p>
  */}
  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>Write to <a href="mailto:hello@pumpos.app?subject=Privacy%20question">hello@pumpos.app</a> with any privacy question.</p>

  <h2>Visiting this website</h2>
  <p>This website is a set of static pages served by Cloudflare. Our pages set no cookies and load no analytics, advertising or tracking scripts. Fonts and images come from this site, and the site search runs in your browser. Cloudflare receives the technical details of each request, such as your IP address and browser, in order to deliver the page.</p>

  <h2>Asking for a demo</h2>
  {DEMO_BOOKING_URL ? (
    <p>The demo form sends your name, phone number, station name and town, and any tank, nozzle and attendant counts you enter, to our booking calendar so you can choose a time. The calendar provider is <span class="legal-tbd">To be confirmed</span>.</p>
  ) : (
    <p>The demo form does not send anything to our servers. It opens WhatsApp with a message to us containing your name, phone number, station name and town, and any tank, nozzle and attendant counts you entered. Nothing reaches us until you press send. You can also write to us at hello@pumpos.app instead.</p>
  )}
  <p>If you message us on WhatsApp, WhatsApp (Meta) carries the conversation and your number. The WhatsApp links on this site go through our own <code>/whatsapp</code> page, which only forwards you to WhatsApp.</p>
  <p>We use what you send to reply, arrange the demo and talk about the pilot. Please don't send customer lists, bank statements or other records. The demo uses sample data.</p>

  <h2>Demo stations</h2>
  <p>For a hands-on demo we may create a sample station filled with sample data. If you give us an email address, PumpOS sends you a sign-in invitation for that station. Each demo has an expiry date that we set when we create it. On that date its logins stop working. Seven days later PumpOS deletes the demo organisation, its sample records and its logins. We can extend a demo if you ask.</p>

  <h2>Pilot stations</h2>
  <p>Once a station joins the pilot, its team enters operational records into PumpOS: shifts, nozzle readings, sales, stock, collections, expenses and credit customers. These records include personal details that the station chooses to add, such as staff names, phone numbers and email addresses, and the names and contact details of its credit customers.</p>
  <p>Each organisation's records are kept apart from every other organisation's. Inside an organisation, the role the owner gives each user decides what that user can see and do. PumpOS staff access a station's records only when needed to set up or support it.</p>
  <p>The station decides how the staff and customer details it enters are used. PumpOS stores and processes them on the station's behalf, to run the service for that station.</p>

  <h2>Providers that handle data</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Cloudflare.</strong> Hosts this website, the web console, the mobile web app and the PumpOS API, and connects the API to the database.</li>
    <li><strong>Supabase.</strong> Hosts the database that holds station records, and runs sign-in, including the sign-in invitation emails.</li>
    <li><strong>GitHub.</strong> Serves the desktop app download and its update checks. Each check sends GitHub a normal web request from your computer.</li>
    <li><strong>WhatsApp (Meta).</strong> Only if you choose to message us there.</li>
    <li><strong>Google (Gmail).</strong> Receives email sent to hello@pumpos.app.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>The database is in Supabase's Mumbai region, in India. We have not confirmed where the other providers process data. We make no claim about certifications or compliance standards.</p>

  {/* Hidden until retention periods are decided.
  <h2>How long we keep data</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Demo stations: deleted seven days after the demo expires, as described above.</li>
    <li>Demo requests by email and WhatsApp messages: <span class="legal-tbd">To be confirmed</span>.</li>
    <li>Pilot station records: kept while the organisation uses PumpOS. Export and deletion when a station leaves: <span class="legal-tbd">To be confirmed</span>.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Ask us before your station joins and we will confirm these points in writing.</p>
  */}

  <h2>Your requests</h2>
  <p>To see, correct or delete information you have sent us, email <a href="mailto:hello@pumpos.app?subject=Privacy%20request">hello@pumpos.app</a>. If you work at a pilot station, ask your station's owner first: they control the records your station keeps in PumpOS. We reply within 14 days.</p>
  <p>Grievance contact: Abdullah Nettoor, <a href="mailto:hello@pumpos.app?subject=Privacy%20grievance">hello@pumpos.app</a>.</p>

  <h2>Still open before publication</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Legal operator details, after registration.</li>
    <li>Retention periods, and the export and deletion process when a station leaves.</li>
    <li>Review against applicable Indian privacy law.</li>
    <li>Effective date and revision date.</li>
  </ul>
</ProseLayout>
